<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuelan money supply falls in week to Aug 9.</title>
<headline>Venezuelan money supply falls in week to Aug 9.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuelan money supply, as measured by the monetary aggregate M-2, fell 2.68 percent to 4.250 trillion bolivars in the week to August 9, the central bank said.</p>
<p>At the beginning of 1996, M-2 was 3.530 trillion bolivars.</p>
<p>The monetary base fell 4.91 percent, or 59 billion bolivars, to 1.480 trillion bolivars in the week to August 9.</p>
<p>-- Caracas Newsroom 582 834405</p>
</text>
